From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-aims: drop one conference member at a time

A HANGUP aimed at a leg the CP has swallowed into a conference is
dropped without an answer, and one aimed at the conference ends the
whole call -- so neither can hang up a single member. The captured
Android dialler uses CONF_CALL_ADD_REMOVE_USER (0x0d12) instead: one
frame, REMOVE, the conference's call id, and the member named by both
its own call id and its number. The CP answered status 0 and republished
the conference with its party count down by one.

Layout from RilReqConfCallAddRemoveUser.getBytes() in ShannonIms.apk,
and the test reproduces the captured 534-byte frame byte for byte.

